# Copy to .env and fill in. Compose and `uv run` both pick it up.
#
# Only variables the code actually reads are listed. Every one below is optional -- the
# defaults in src/ are correct for a local checkout, so an empty .env works.

# --- Serving (src/api/main.py) ---
# Where to load each track's model from. Registry alias by default; the Docker image
# overrides this to the baked-in /app/model so `docker run` needs no MLflow server.
#
# Per-track, because there are two registered models with independent retrain cadence:
# riskwatch_credit and riskwatch_fraud. MODEL_URI_<TRACK> wins over the shared MODEL_URI,
# which exists only for single-track deployments and can name just one of them.
MODEL_URI_CREDIT=models:/riskwatch_credit@production
# The fraud track lands in W2; its MODEL_URI_FRAUD entry is added when the model is
# actually registered, not before -- a URI naming an unregistered model is a boot failure
# waiting for someone to uncomment it.
# Only consulted when MODEL_URI is a local path -- a path gives the API no way to look the
# version up, and /health would otherwise report "unknown".
# MODEL_VERSION=
# No DECISION_THRESHOLD here. The serving cut is no longer a single number: decide()
# in src/api/main.py reads the per-track DECISION_BANDS (a review band between two
# operating points), so an env var could only ever set one of two thresholds for one
# of two tracks. Leaving it documented would advertise a knob that does nothing.

# --- Tracking (src/models/train.py, src/api/main.py) ---
# Defaults to sqlite:///<repo>/mlflow.db, anchored to the repo root rather than the CWD.
# Point it at the compose service (http://mlflow:5000) to use the server instead.
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=

# --- Prediction log (src/api/prediction_log.py) ---
# Defaults to <repo>/logs/predictions.jsonl.
# PREDICTION_LOG_PATH=

# --- Drift (src/monitoring/drift.py) ---
# Defaults to localhost:9091, which inside a container is the container itself. The dev
# and compose services set this to pushgateway:9091.
# PUSHGATEWAY_URL=localhost:9091

# --- Airflow (docker-compose.airflow.yml) ---
# Required -- compose refuses to start without them, rather than falling back to a default
# that would be a committed credential.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
AIRFLOW_ADMIN_USER=admin
AIRFLOW_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me
# On Linux only: export AIRFLOW_UID=$(id -u) so containers do not write root-owned files.
AIRFLOW_UID=50000

# --- GCP ---
# Nothing in src/ reads these yet. They belong to Milestone 3, which is not built and not
# currently decided; see STATUS.md. Left here as the shape a deploy would need.
# GCP_PROJECT_ID=
# GCS_BUCKET=
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=
